The Späti is very bright.
I am looking for a gift for my family.
I find a bar of chocolate.
It is from Germany.
I go to the counter.
A cashier stands there.
"That comes to three Euro," he says.
I pay the three Euro.
I take the chocolate.
Then I go to the door.
Suddenly, the cashier calls out.
"Excuse me!" he calls loudly.
I stop.
"Is that your bag?" he asks.
I look back at the counter.
Oh no, my bag is lying there.
"Yes, that is my bag," I say.
"Thank you very much!"
The cashier smiles.
I take the bag and go back to my flat.
